Subject: Aria: no directory descriptor on OpenVMS

translog_init opens the log directory to fsync it after creating and
deleting log files. OpenVMS cannot open() a directory ('File .../DATA/ not
found', Aria engine: log initialization failed), so skip it as on Windows:
directory_fd stays -1 and every sync_dir() call already passes
MY_IGNORE_BADFD. mysys only syncs directories on Linux
(NEED_EXPLICIT_SYNC_DIR).

--- a/storage/maria/ma_loghandler.c	2026-10-05 08:04:29.643243723 +0100
+++ b/storage/maria/ma_loghandler.c	2026-10-05 08:04:29.664641341 +0100
@@ -3678,7 +3678,8 @@
 
   /* Directory to store files */
   unpack_dirname(log_descriptor.directory, directory);
-#ifndef _WIN32
+  /* Neither Windows nor OpenVMS can open() a directory to sync it. */
+#if !defined(_WIN32) && !defined(__VMS)
   if ((log_descriptor.directory_fd= my_open(log_descriptor.directory,
                                             O_RDONLY, MYF(MY_WME))) < 0)
   {
